---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="How devsyllabus Cites Sources | devsyllabus"
  description="Our source citation policy: which authorities we cite, how references appear on each page, and how external links are handled."
  path="/sources/"
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Editorial Policy', href: '/editorial-policy/' }, { label: 'Sources' }]} />

  <div class="doc">
  <h1>How we cite sources</h1>

  <h2>References on every technical page</h2>
  <p>
    Study notes and technical articles end with a references section
    listing the sources the content rests on. Where a source is publicly
    linkable, such as an RFC or official documentation, the reference
    links to it; books are cited by title, edition, and publisher.
  </p>

  <h2>Inline citation practice</h2>
  <p>
    Claims that follow directly from a cited source are covered by the
    references section. Claims that are narrower or more specific — a
    particular section of a standard, a specific table — are attributed
    inline in the text.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>External links point to primary sources, not to aggregator pages.</li>
    <li>
      We do not sell or rent links, and external links are never a
      condition of coverage.
    </li>
    <li>
      External links open in the same tab and are marked plainly in the
      references list. We are not responsible for the content of external
      sites — see our <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>See also the <a href="/fact-checking/">fact-checking process</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
